 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.

+## Filtering
+
+The view has a name filter and a status filter above the grid, and a line
+reporting how many customers match. Both filters are applied by the repository,
+so the grid keeps holding one page of rows and the matching count keeps coming
+from a count query. The name filter is split on whitespace into terms, and every
+term has to be a substring of the first or the last name, ignoring case and
+accents.
+
+The filter lives in the URL as the query parameters `name` and `status`, for
+example `/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`, so a narrowed list can be bookmarked
+or sent to a colleague. Editing a filter replaces the current history entry
